List of accessibility features to include on a website:

background and foreground colors and text with enough puntuation so that it can be read on any type of screen no matter the lighting.

headings have to be in the correct order.

specify sematic elements (like page header) for the screen reader.

use WAI-ARIA elements to specify parts for screen readers (tables.)

alt text on pictures for screen readers and has to specify in a simple way what the picture is showing.

have to specify links and make them in short words for screen readers, links also need different colors for different actions and to be underlined for colorblindess.

text that is simple and gets to the point.
